* ngspice startup options. MUST live in the directory ngspice RUNS FROM.
*
* OpenRAM writes its own copy of this into /tmp/openram_*_temp/, which only
* works if ngspice's cwd is that temp dir. run_openram.sh cds here instead, so
* without this file all three settings below are silently dropped - no error,
* just a ~15x slower run. Measured on an identical 150 ns stimulus with
* ngspice-41: 24.7 min with these options, >6.5 h without them.
*
* num_threads   - OpenMP parallelism (one thread otherwise; watch %CPU to tell)
* ngbehavior    - HSPICE/spice3 compatibility, needed for the sky130 models
* ng_nomodcheck - skip model parameter range checks; expensive across thousands
*                 of BSIM4 instances
set num_threads=3
set ngbehavior=hsa
set ng_nomodcheck
